66
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.083
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:58.404
Visal, what does self-advocacy mean?

68
00:03:59.517 --> 00:04:04.758
It means speaking up for yourself. It is important to voice your opinion respectfully.

69
00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.246
Have you ever done it?

70
00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:14.311
Yes. It was hard to tell my teacher I needed more time, but I did.

71
00:04:15.417 --> 00:04:16.418
How did it go?

72
00:04:17.517 --> 00:04:22.352
Well! It is easier to get help when you ask clearly and politely.

73
00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.244
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:29.093
Grammar focus: Cleft sentences for emphasis.

75
00:04:29.393 --> 00:04:30.626
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:34.129
It is important to voice your opinion respectfully.

77
00:04:35.017 --> 00:04:36.807
It was hard to ask for help.

78
00:04:37.717 --> 00:04:39.205
It is your right to say no.

79
00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:45.756
Start with 'It is' + adjective, then 'to' + verb. This puts the focus on your main idea.

80
00:04:46.517 --> 00:04:50.434
Be careful! Don't say: It is important voice your opinion.

81
00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.166
Say: It is important to voice your opinion.

82
00:04:55.466 --> 00:04:58.185
After 'It is important', use 'to' + verb.

83
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.641
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:03.400
Speaking Up.

85
00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.605
Self-advocacy means standing up for yourself.

86
00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.412
It is important to voice your opinion respectfully.

87
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.060
