90
00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:28.541
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:29.383 --> 00:05:31.545
It is important blank voice your opinion.

92
00:05:31.845 --> 00:05:34.500
A, to. B, for. C, that.

93
00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:39.497
The answer is A: to.

94
00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.079
The freedom to make your own decisions is blank.

95
00:05:43.379 --> 00:05:47.485
A, autonomy. B, advocacy. C, negotiation.

96
00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:53.207
The answer is A: autonomy.

97
00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.615
Making clear limits to protect yourself is boundary-blank.

98
00:05:57.915 --> 00:06:01.952
A, setting. B, making. C, taking.

99
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:07.198
The answer is A: setting.

100
00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.447
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:12.283 --> 00:06:15.560
Describe a time you advocated for yourself or someone else.

102
00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.699
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:25.999 --> 00:06:34.921
Last year, a classmate was left out of our group. It was important to include her, so I spoke to the teacher, and she joined us.

104
00:06:35.221 --> 00:06:36.896
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:37.783 --> 00:06:42.444
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and cleft sentences for emphasis.

106
00:06:42.744 --> 00:06:46.395
Today's value is courage. Try new things and be brave.

107
00:06:46.695 --> 00:06:48.883
